document.write('Bottle-fed babies who ate solid foods before the age of 4 months were six times more likely to be obese at the age of 3 years than those that started later, said US researchers who also found that the timing of solid food introduction made no difference in the case of breastfed babies. You can read how Dr Susanna Y Huh of the Division of Gastroenterology, Children\'s Hospital Boston, Massachusetts, and colleagues, carried out their study, in the March issue of Pediatrics, the journal of the American Academy of Pediatrics (AAP)...');
